## 2. Decisions the Evidence Supports

The purpose of the analysis is to turn historical supporter behaviour into practical retention decisions.

| Business decision | Analytical evidence | Proposed action |
|---|---|---|
| **WHO — Who should receive additional attention?** | Repeat-giving propensity ranking | Test additional retention attention within priority groups. |
| **WHAT — What could make communication more relevant?** | First-gift product, amount, channel and prior relationship | Test context-based communication against the standard journey. |
| **WHEN — When should re-engagement occur?** | Historical time to second gift | Compare selected first-year and anniversary contact windows. |
| **WHERE — Which acquisition journey needs investigation?** | Channel-level repeat rates and product comparisons | Audit Retail Stand onboarding and contact quality before testing journey changes. |

These decisions could involve fundraising, supporter retention, CRM and analytics teams. Operational ownership, resources and feasibility would require confirmation before implementation.

