## 3. What the Project Measures

Consistent business rules are essential to avoid misleading repeat-giving comparisons.

| Definition | Analytical rule |
|---|---|
| **Unit of analysis** | One supporter |
| **First giving occasion** | First observed qualifying gift date. Qualifying transactions on the same day are grouped into one giving occasion. |
| **First-gift value** | Sum of qualifying transactions on the first giving date. |
| **Repeat outcome** | Another qualifying one-off gift on a later date within 24 months. |
| **Follow-up requirement** | Supporters must have a complete 24-month observation window. |
| **Transaction exclusions** | BounceBack transactions (`BB`, `BB COMSPON`, `BB COST REC`) are excluded because they belong to a different giving context. |
| **Supporter exclusions** | Supporters with active ongoing commitments at the first qualifying occasion are excluded. Eligible former ongoing supporters are retained. |
| **Predictive population** | WVA-classified Mass acquisition supporters. |
| **Prediction point** | End of the first giving occasion, using information available at or before that point. |

### Analytical Scope

The project uses two related but distinct analytical populations.

| Population | Supporters | Purpose |
|---|---:|---|
| **Descriptive cohort** | 19,194 | Understand repeat-giving patterns, supporter characteristics and timing. |
| **Final Mass test cohort** | 6,741 | Evaluate how effectively the predictive model ranks future repeat-giving outcomes retrospectively. |

The descriptive cohort covers first qualifying gifts from **17 March 2021 to 17 March 2024**, using data ending **17 March 2026**.

The final Mass test cohort covers first qualifying gifts during **2023 to 17 March 2024**.

**Out of scope:** Campaign execution, production deployment, causal attribution and supporter lifetime-value prediction were not completed as part of this project.

